;;; Mini CMUdict fixture. Same format as the real dictionary (BSD-2-Clause):
;;; WORD  P1 P2 P3, two spaces before the phonemes; WORD(n) for alternates.
;;; Every entry here backs a row in the verdict table or the guardrail table.
ATE  EY1 T
EIGHT  EY1 T
LATE  L EY1 T
COLLATE  K AH0 L EY1 T
IMPREGNATE  IH0 M P R EH1 G N EY2 T
ADJUDICATE  AH0 JH UW1 D IH0 K EY2 T
DEFENESTRATE  D IH0 F EH1 N AH0 S T R EY2 T
OBJURGATE  AA1 B JH ER0 G EY2 T
CHOCOLATE  CH AO1 K L AH0 T
COMMENSURATE  K AH0 M EH1 N S ER0 AH0 T
HAT  HH AE1 T
SATE  S EY1 T
READ  R IY1 D
READ(1)  R EH1 D
BED  B EH1 D
TEAR  T IH1 R
TEAR(1)  T EH1 R
BEER  B IH1 R
CARE  K EH1 R
KATE  K EY1 T
GATE  G EY1 T
GATES  G EY1 T S
PLATES  P L EY1 T S
;;; The `-ate` guardrails: an unstressed schwa in the final syllable, which no
;;; normalisation may erase (see docs/adr/0010, and CHOCOLATE/COMMENSURATE above).
PRIVATE  P R AY1 V AH0 T
CLIMATE  K L AY1 M AH0 T
SENATE  S EH1 N AH0 T
ACCURATE  AE1 K Y ER0 AH0 T
;;; The cot-caught merger: AO words that must join their AA counterparts.
DOCKED  D AA1 K T
TALKED  T AO1 K T
WALKED  W AO1 K T
BALKED  B AO1 K T
STALKED  S T AO1 K T
HAWKED  HH AO1 K T
;;; Pre-lateral position is merged too — `ball` rhymes with `doll`.
BALL  B AO1 L
DOLL  D AA1 L
;;; Pre-rhotic position is not merged. These three pairs are the guardrail.
FOR  F AO1 R
FAR  F AA1 R
BORN  B AO1 R N
BARN  B AA1 R N
CORD  K AO1 R D
CARD  K AA1 R D
